B.dpn=new A.u("Rooms, recording, takes and the Open Mic cost us almost nothing to run, so they are free and will stay free \u2014 charging for them would be charging for the reason to open the app.\n\nA call and a question to Clef cost us money every time, and so does a song sheet. The full analysis is where a sheet's money goes. It runs on a graphics card we rent by the second, which pulls the instruments apart to hear the words off the singing, finds the beat and the bars, names the parts, and keeps every instrument as its own track to solo, mute or play along with. More machine time and more storage, every song, which is what you would be paying for.\n\nThe free one, the chords sheet, does not use the card. It sends the recording to our chord model as it is and gives you the chords and the key, with no words or bar lines.\n\nThat is also why a full analysis uses a credit, and why running it again on a recording that has had one does not: the second time is ours.\n\nUntil Studio opens, video on calls is on for everyone. When it opens, video comes with Studio, and one person on Studio brings it to everyone on a call in their band. Sound is on every plan.\n\nKeeping what you record costs a little for every month it is kept, which is why each plan has a space. Nothing is deleted for being over it, and nothing is deleted by a clock.",null,B.dhr,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,B.eeQ)
