B.b96=new A.cH("record",B.kI,"How do I record something?","Press REC, the record key in the bar at the foot of the four main screens: Your music, Open Mic, Messages and Learn. On a wider screen, a tablet held sideways or a computer, the bar has no REC: press New idea instead. On other screens, press More, then Everything else, then Record an idea. It starts a new idea \u2014 no naming, no choosing where it lives. You can do both afterwards, once there is something worth filing.\n\nThe first time, it asks to use the microphone. Then it counts 3, 2, 1 and records; press Start now if you are ready sooner. To record from the tap with no count, press Tools in the recorder and turn off Count in before recording.\n\nPress Stop and save when you have it. It is saved in Ideas at once, and the page shows how long it is, with Hear it, Record again (which keeps this one and starts another) and Throw away (with Undo). Done takes you back to where you were.\n\nOn a phone it works with no signal: the recording is kept on the phone first, and goes into Your music by itself when there is signal. One recording runs for up to 12 minutes, which is as long as a song here can hold, and the recorder says so in the last minute.\n\nIf the idea is words and there is nowhere quiet to sing, press Tools in the recorder and then Write it down. It is also under More on Your music, and under More in Ideas. On a phone what you type is kept on the phone as you type it, and goes into Ideas as a song named from its first line when you press Done, or by itself once there is signal.\n\nTo add a recording to a song you already have, open it and press Record it, the gold at the foot. Once the song has a recording, the same gold says Record a take. On a computer, with a song open beside Your music, the gold button says Record, or New take once the song has a recording; with no song open it says New idea.",B.cyE)
B.dK=new A.Gj("Songs and takes",1,"songsAndTakes")
B.er8=s(["workspace_layers_button","layers_record_button"],t.s)
B.bXz=s(["take","takes","another","add","overdub","layer","part","second","share","shared","song"],t.s)
B.b99=new A.cH("take",B.dK,"How do I add a take to a song?","Open the song and press Record a take, the gold button at the foot (Record it, if the song has no recording yet). Takes opens, counts you in, and records over the song while it plays; press Stop when you are done. To come in partway, tap the song's bar on Takes where you want to start, and press Record from there.\n\nA take stays private to you until you share it. Tap it on Takes, press Tools, and press Share for the one you want the room to hear \u2014 nothing you have not shared is ever audible to anybody, including on the Open Mic. The same Tools takes it back, or takes it off the song.\n\nWith no signal, a take is kept on the phone and shown on Takes as On this phone, not sent yet; tap it for Try again. It goes up by itself when there is signal. If a take sounds late, tap it, press Tools, then Volume and timing, and press Line it up to move it while it plays.",B.bXz)
B.esG=s(["workspace_analyze_button","choose_reference_recording"],t.s)
B.c51=s(["chord","chords","sheet","lyrics","words","key","tempo","bpm","transcribe","transcription","tab","analyse","analyze","notation","song"],t.s)
B.b8q=new A.cH("sheet",B.dK,"How do I get the chords and words for my song?","Record something first, then open the song and press Song Sheet, and choose one.\n\nChords is free: the chords and the key, with no words or bar lines. The full analysis also writes down the words you sang and puts the chords over them, finds the tempo and the bars, and names the parts; it uses a credit, takes a few minutes, and keeps going if you leave the screen.",B.c51)
